{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":74,"recorded_at":1780531400000143,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4ac-1cb1-7451-b8bb-c14745a4c665"},"task_id":"01a0c4ac-1cb1-7451-b8bb-c14745a4c665","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4ac-1cb1-7451-b8bb-c14745a4c665","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev5.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev4.md and every earlier precondition. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-35urbp, the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i. Revision 4 was reviewed by RUN-260921-30d48f (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with **no P1**: two P2 and two P3. Read TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev4.md first. The reviewer states that **every rev3 finding — P2-A/B/C, P3-A..E and the four observations — is closed with driven evidence and stays closed**, including the §3.2 path, the background absence code and the running-server entry pins. Keep all of it. **Production behaves correctly at every point this review drove.** What remains is a test ORACLE that cannot see the defect, one entry surface that re-opens a closed divergence, and two prose/axis items. This is the last round I expect; make it complete.\n3|Trunk has NOT moved (base is still 799c338). Your working tree is the rev4 candidate; build revision 5 on it. Do not refresh, do not rebase.\n4|\n5|1. **P2-A — your custody assertions cannot see the wrapper, so the new classification gate has no narrowing that admits what it must reject.** `runtimeAbsent` (acquire.go:246-252) remaps only the verify-side `runtime absent` detail to the typed `capability_unavailable`; every unsafe-leaf refusal must keep its custody code (SPEC 810-812, TRACEABILITY row 52, README). You shipped `N-background-absence-remap`, which weakens the gate to REJECT a member it must accept — that pins one direction. The DoD narrowing is the other direction, and it survives: widening the gate to `(local.Detail == \"runtime absent\" || local.Detail == \"runtime mode\")` makes a widened 0755 leaf on the background path return `capability_unavailable` with the custody `*Error` hidden as its cause, and **the full committed suite passes in both passes**. The reason is the oracle: `requireLocalError` (tmuxserver_test.go:79-91) uses `errors.As`, and `axerror.Error.Unwrap` returns the cause, so a `backgroundUnavailable(req, verr)` wrapping a custody `*Error` still satisfies an assertion for `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir` / `runtime mode`. All three tests that are supposed to pin the custody half assert through that helper, so none of them observes the code the caller actually renders — and the cause is redacted off the wire by design, so the wrapper IS the observable refusal. Fix the oracle first: make `requireLocalError` assert the TOP-LEVEL dynamic type (`err.(*Error)`, or additionally that no `*axerror.Error` is reachable), so every custody assertion pins what a caller sees. Then ship `N-absence-remap-widen` in that widening shape and keep `N-background-absence-remap` for the other direction. Re-run every custody row after the oracle change and report any that only passed because of the old helper.\n6|2. **P2-B — `Request.Name` re-opens the §3.2 divergence on every call.** Rev3's path fix was closed at the constants, and `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` pins them — but through the production entry the derived socket is `<Root>/<Name>/ax.sock` with `Name` a free grammar-checked segment \"(usually RuntimeDirName)\". `Acquire` with `Name` = `ax-tmux`, `default` or `tmux-502` spawns at `<root>/ax-tmux/ax.sock`, `<root>/default/ax.sock`, `<root>/tmux-502/ax.sock` and no gate refuses — `default` being the very conventional name row 22 refuses as an override. Replacing `req.Name` with `RuntimeDirName` at the `Acquire` lexical step SURVIVED both passes, because every committed `Acquire` test passes the constant: the field's variability is unmeasured through the entry. There is no production reason for it to vary — the exported `EnsureRuntimeDir`/`VerifyRuntimeDir` need a `name` parameter for the grammar rows, the acquisition entry does not. Either drop `Request.Name` and have `Acquire` pass `RuntimeDirName`, or refuse `req.Name != RuntimeDirName` at `Acquire` with an entry test and a narrowing row. Either way add the entry-level assertion that `Acquire`'s outcome socket equals `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock`, for both the foreground and background callers, and name it under rows 16/56.\n7|3. **P3-A — the absence remap is pinned on the macOS axis only.** Narrowing it to `runtimeAbsent(verr) && req.Platform == scalar.PlatformMacOS` SURVIVED both passes: `validRequest` defaults to macOS and no committed absence test uses Linux or WSL2, so a Linux background restore worker with an absent leaf — the same cold state, since `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is tmpfs — would get the custody code instead of `capability_unavailable`. Row 29 pins the Linux BROKER miss, not the absence arm. Add Linux and WSL2 subtests to `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` and name them under row 52.\n8|4. **P3-B — a censusable \"every\" that is false.** README and acquire.go:135-137 both say \"every background test arms a spy spawner that fails the run if it is ever invoked\". Census of the 11 background-path `Acquire` tests: 7 arm the spy, 4 do not (`TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid`, `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf`, the background half of `TestAcquireRefusesMissingDependencies`, the background iteration of `TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform`). With `Spawn` nil, a guarded plant of the exact `D-background-fallback` shape is invisible to those four. Arm the spy in all four, or reword both sites to the claim that is true.\n9|5. **The reviewer's five observations — take each as a one-sentence TRACEABILITY entry, they are cheap and they close the file.** (a) The ELOOP-as-absent mutant survives because it is darwin-equivalent: on this host `openat(O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY)` on a symlink leaf returns `ENOTDIR`, so the ELOOP arm is unreachable and the configured suite is darwin-only; on Linux the same open returns `ELOOP`, which production maps to containment — reasoned, not run. Say that under rows 6/13. (b) An unopenable 0000 root reports `runtime root` rather than `runtime containment` under a mutant, refusal-to-refusal, with no committed test staging it — report under B15 as an error-arm row. (c) The `Fchmod`, `Fsync` and leaf `Stat` failure arms are the same unstageable class and are missing from B15's list — add them. (d) An `ax` invocation from inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller populates `Ambient` from the process environment: over-strict rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes, but say so under row 23 or B16 and name TASK-260830-1c28dz as the leaf that decides it deliberately. (e) Of the five collision members only `TMUXEnv` and `InheritedSocket` can name the derived socket — state that scoping where row 23 makes its claim.\n10|\n11|PROCESS. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED; exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept, and do NOT touch `internal/traceability` — the final leaf g0pcnt carries the registry. Run your own package tests, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (keep it green), and the harness BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once, reading the commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` in the candidate config. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, MANIFEST with no self-entry, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, zero `__pycache__`), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` so revision 5 is constructed, and exit promptly. Report the ratio you MEASURE. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 5.\n12|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n13|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n14|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n15|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n16|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n17|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n18|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n19|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.","final_result":true}}}
