{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c70f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":482,"recorded_at":1780531400000959,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4ad-3ba7-7372-8638-9f6196f2f037"},"task_id":"01a0c4ad-3ba7-7372-8638-9f6196f2f037","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4ad-3ba7-7372-8638-9f6196f2f037","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t35rev4/matrix-rev4.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp conformance matrix — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev4)\n2|\n3|Authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Every row names the\n4|spec clause in the spec's own words, the production call site, and the\n5|named committed test that drives it through that entry. 58 of 58 rows\n6|driven (row 55 extends the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth\n7|ambient member; row 56 binds the Section 3.2 path and runtime-root\n8|clause; rows 57-58 pin the commit-failure and whitespace-override\n9|arms). Bounds B1-B21 are stated in\n10|`internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`. Changes from rev3: row 10/13\n11|name the aligned missing-root code, row 13 names the absence detail,\n12|row 16 pins the spec path literals, row 23 covers the TMUX real\n13|encoding, row 42 covers admission-empty running servers, row 52 names\n14|the background absence/missing-root/custody split, rows 56-58 are new,\n15|and the mutant map carries eight new narrowing rows.\n16|\n17|Attestation authority: sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n18|verification, liveness, and expiry are the landed\n19|`internal/terminalbackend` Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission verdict,\n20|consumed here as an `Admitted` set composed only with the generation\n21|equality `internal/axpane` checkRealm enforces. This leaf decides\n22|membership plus generation binding and re-decides nothing.\n23|\n24|## §3.2 socket path and runtime root\n25|\n26|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n27||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n28|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Request` contract (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir |\n29|\n30|## §4.2 dedicated -S server; no ambient/default discovery or reuse\n31|\n32|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n33||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n34|| 16 | AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server, as `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` with both leaves asserted as spec literals | `SocketPath` (socket.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir |\n35|| 17 | MUST NOT discover or reuse the default server by ambient socket name, under hostile ambient on all five members | `ResolveSocket` (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n36|| 18 | Ambient facts observed without use | `ObserveAmbient` (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n37|| 19 | Environment-variable vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable |\n38|| 20 | Inherited-socket vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket |\n39|| 21 | Default-path vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path |\n40|| 22 | Conventional-name vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name |\n41|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR vector refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir |\n42|| 58 | Whitespace-only override refuses with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/whitespace_only, TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector/whitespace_only |\n43|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member, byte-identical and unclean (`/./`, `//`) spellings alike, and the TMUX member in the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings (2 subtests), TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling, TestResolveSocketRefusesTMUXEnvRealEncoding, TestAcquireRefusesTMUXEnvCollisionRealEncoding |\n44|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector | `Acquire` via `BuildArgv` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n45|| 41 | Running attested dedicated server attaches with no second spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n46|| 46 | Spawn vector carries the dedicated -S socket | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n47|| 47 | Ambient sockets refuse at the spawn vector on all five members | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n48|\n49|## §4.2 credential-sensitive creation; background broker-or-refuse\n50|\n51|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n52||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n53|| 24 | A background CLI MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server (macOS) | `Acquire` via `CheckBrokerCo