ing table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\n25|\n26|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n27||---|---|---|---|\n28|| P2-A derived path is not the spec path (`<root>/ax-tmux/ax-tmux.sock` vs `<root>/tmux/ax.sock`) | `RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"`, `SocketName = \"ax.sock\"`; `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` asserts both spec literals plus the joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock`; `Request.Root` documented as the Runtime IPC root resolved by the landed `localstore` layout as `PathRuntime` (no second resolution); new §3.2 row 56 in TRACEABILITY and the matrix; README/doc.go updated; `stateRoot` helper and `ax-state` fixtures renamed to runtime roots | `TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir` (literal mismatch on any renamed constant) | `pkg-tests-v.log`, `internal/tmuxserver/socket.go`, `runtime.go`, `acquire.go` |\n29|| P2-B background + absent runtime dir returns a custody code, not `capability_unavailable` | The background path maps the absent leaf to the typed `capability_unavailable` with the request's realm/readiness details (no broker probe, no spawn, no directory write); an existing-but-unsafe leaf keeps its custody code. `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` rewritten to assert the typed refusal + details + no directory + zero spawns; new `TestAcquireBackgroundMissingRootRefusesInvalid`; narrowings `N-verify-absence-detail` (verify arm) and `N-background-absence-remap` (remap arm); README \"otherwise returns\" and rows 13/52 fixed | `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` (custody code under either mutant), `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence` (containment detail under the verify mutant) | `harness-pass1/N-verify-absence-detail.log`, `harness-pass1/N-background-absence-remap.log` (+ pass 2) |\n30|| P2-C Running arm pinned at the entry only for servers with admission data | Committed `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesRunningWithEmptyAdmission` (Running + `RealmAdmission{}` → `server attestation