gence states the umask\n151|bound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\n152|lifecycle leaf (bound B9).\n153|\n154|## Validation (all run firsthand in this session)\n155|\n156|Configured suite read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`\n157|(count 30, verified by read). All 30 green, run by this run (nothing\n158|accepted from rev3 or from construction):\n159|\n160|- 1 gofmt clean (empty file list); 2 `go build ./...` exit 0;\n161|  3 `go vet ./...` exit 0.\n162|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v` exit 0: 45/45 packages ok, 0 package\n163|  FAIL, 0 unindented test FAIL (the 21 indented `--- FAIL` lines are\n164|  mutant-kill excerpts logged by the passing resumesmoke suite), 14\n165|  pre-existing SKIP outside this package, 0 SKIP in\n166|  `internal/tmuxserver`.\n167|- 5 race gate exit 0 with no DATA RACE: run in 6 bounded groups\n168|  (8/8/8/8/8/5 packages = all 45 from `go list ./...`) because one\n169|  shell call is time-bounded; same flags otherwise (`-race -count=1`).\n170|  45/45 ok.\n171|- 6 `go test ./... -cover -count=1` exit 0: 45/45 ok.\n172|  `go test ./internal/tmuxserver/ -cover` 92.6% statements.\n173|- 7-23 all 17 fuzz seeds exit 0. 24 tracecheck exit 0 (70/574).\n174|  25 cataloggen -check exit 0. 26 linux build exit 0. 27 windows build\n175|  exit 0. 28 JSON parse exit 0. 29 `task-board validate` exit 0 (with\n176|  the board's pre-existing 180 issues). 30 `git diff --check` exit 0.\n177|- Repository gates beyond the 30: `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet\n178|  ./...` exit 0, `GOOS=windows go test -c ./internal/tmuxserver`\n179|  exit 0, `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0; package\n180|  suite 134 RUN / 70 top-level PASS / 64 subtest PASS / 0 SKIP;\n181|  tmux-hidden suite (`PATH` without tmux, `TMUX`/`TMUX_TMPDIR` unset,\n182|  no tmux process) exit 0 with 70 top-level PASS and 0 SKIP.\n183|\n184|Reran myself: everything above, plus the mutant battery (targeted\n185|subsets during development + two full