{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c815","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":613,"recorded_at":1780531400001221,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"call_id":"call_01a0c4adb3c777d19d8a665469c504ad","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/doc.go`.\n1|// Package tmuxserver owns AX private tmux server management: owner-only\n2|// runtime directories and dedicated tmux -S servers with no ambient or\n3|// default-server discovery or reuse. It is the first leaf of the\n4|// production-tmux-backend story.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 3.2 (platform paths: the\n7|// dedicated socket `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n8|// root — the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity) and\n9|// Section 4.2 (tmux backend, dedicated -S server,\n10|// credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse,\n11|// launchctl managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations\n12|// never authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for\n13|// the wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence\n14|// cited landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only\n15|// and non-replicable).\n16|//\n17|// Division of authority (composed, never forked): the caller vocabulary\n18|// (foreground/background) comes from internal/axpane, which already\n19|// gates the wrapper decision over it; the capability_unavailable typed\n20|// refusal comes from internal/axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable, which\n21|// enforces the exact Section 15.3 detail set; the attestation verdict\n22|// comes from the landed internal/terminalbackend admission\n23|// (Reconcile/ResolveEvidence), consumed here as an Admitted set\n24|// composed only with the generation equality the wrapper owner\n25|// already enforces — sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n26|// verification, liveness, and expiry are the admission's verdict, not\n27|// this leaf's; path grammars come from internal/scalar (absolute root,\n28|// relative member, UUIDv7 session); the Runtime IPC root value comes\n29|// from the landed internal/localstore layout (PathRuntime), resolved\n30|// by the caller and supplied as Request.Root — this leaf resolves no\n31|// root of its own; lexical containment comes from\n32|// internal/secprim.Guard; argv shape validation comes from\n33|// internal/secprim.CheckArgv. What this package owns is the composition\n34|// no landed package provides: the descriptor-relative runtime-directory\n35|// commit (mkdirat from a pinned root handle, not a path-string\n36|// MkdirAll), the three independent custody gates (mode, ownership,\n37|// containment), the five-member ambient non-use proof (TMUX and\n38|// TMUX_TMPDIR environment values, inherited socket, default path,\n39|// conventional name), the background broker-or-refuse acquisition path\n40|// with its no-fallback gate over a typed same-user generation-bound\n41|// broker principal, the foreground ensure-then-attach-or-spawn path,\n42|// and the dedicated -S argv builder.\n43|//\n44|// Bounds: no ax CLI surface, no lifecycle operations (create, attach,\n45|// status, quiesce, stop, terminate, restore belong to the sibling\n46|// leaves), no ConPTY process control, no provider process, no mesh\n47|// transport, and no production probe or spawner implementation —\n48|// caller-supplied probes report the landed admission verdicts, and the\n49|// exec/probe adapters are sibling scope. Native Windows refuses every\n50|// request. No test in this package starts a tmux process: every\n51|// broker, server, and spawner interaction runs through injected\n52|// dependencies, and the suite passes with no tmux installed.\n53|package tmuxserver","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c817","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":614,"recorded_at":1780531400001223,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"call_id":"call_01a0c4adb5a27191871cc29ad68e746c","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/socket.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"path/filepath\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// SocketName is the fixed private socket leaf inside the runtime\n9|// directory: pinned SPEC 806-807 selects the dedicated server by\n10|// `tmux -S <runtime>/tmux/ax.sock`, so the leaf is `ax.sock`. AX\n11|// derives its server socket from this name under the owner-only\n12|// directory and from nothing else.\n13|const SocketName = \"ax.sock\"\n14|\n15|// Ambient environment names the four discovery vectors AX must never\n16|// use. TMUXEnv and TMUXTmpDir name the two environment variables\n17|// whose values may carry an ambient socket; InheritedSocket is a\n18|// socket path handed to the process out of band; DefaultPath is the\n19|// operator default socket path; ConventionalName is the bare\n20|// conventional socket name. No member of this struct ever selects\n21|// the acquisition socket: ResolveSocket derives the socket from the\n22|// runtime directory and refuses any explicit override.\n23|type Ambient struct {\n24|\tTMUXEnv          string\n25|\tTMUXTmpDir       string\n26|\tInheritedSocket  string\n27|\tDefaultPath      string\n28|\tConventionalName string\n29|}\n30|\n31|// Ambient environment variable names. These are the lookup keys the\n32|// caller passes to its own environment function; ObserveAmbient\n33|// records whatever the lookup returns for them without validating\n34|// names or values, because the observation is evidence only and\n35|// resolution never reads it.\n36|const (\n37|\t// EnvTMUX is the tmux(1) session environment variable.\n38|\tEnvTMUX = \"TMUX\"\n39|\t// EnvTMUXTmpDir is the tmux(1) socket-directory override.\n40|\tEnvTMUXTmpDir = \"TMUX_TMPDIR\"\n41|)\n42|\n43|// ConventionalSocketName is the operator default socket leaf that AX\n44|// must never resolve to.\n45|const ConventionalSocketName = \"default\"\n46|\n47|// ObserveAmbient records the ambient socket facts visible to the\n48|// caller without using any of them. The lookup is caller-supplied so\n49|// the production entry never reads the process environment itself:\n50|// ambient discovery cannot hide in an os.Getenv call this package\n51|// never makes. The observation is evidence only; resolution derives\n52|// the socket from the runtime directory and never reads it.\n53|func ObserveAmbient(lookup func(name string) (string, bool), inherited, defPath, conventional string) Ambient {\n54|\tobserved := Ambient{\n55|\t\tInheritedSocket:  inherited,\n56|\t\tDefaultPath:      defPath,\n57|\t\tConventionalName: conventional,\n58|\t}\n59|\tif lookup == nil {\n60|\t\treturn observed\n61|\t}\n62|\tif value, ok := lookup(EnvTMUX); ok {\n63|\t\tobserved.TMUXEnv = value\n64|\t}\n65|\tif value, ok := lookup(EnvTMUXTmpDir); ok {\n66|\t\tobserved.TMUXTmpDir = value\n67|\t}\n68|\treturn observed\n69|}\n70|\n71|// SocketPath derives the dedicated server socket from the runtime\n72|// directory. It is the only socket constructor: acquisition never\n73|// substitutes an ambient value for its result.\n74|func SocketPath(runtimeDir string) string {\n75|\treturn filepath.Join(runtimeDir, SocketName)\n76|}\n77|\n78|// ResolveSocket returns the acquisition socket for the runtime\n79|// directory. An explicit override refuses with the ambient code no\n80|// matter which vector supplied it: there is no override surface,\n81|// only the derived socket. The ambient observation is carried for\n82|// evidence and asserted disjoint from the result by the caller\n83|// tests; resolution never reads it.\n84|func ResolveSocket(runtimeDir string, override string, ambient Ambient) (string, error) {\n85|\tif override != \"\" {\n86|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeAmbientReuse, Detail: \"socket override\"}\n87|\t}\n88|\tsocket := SocketPath(runtimeDir)\n89|\tif err := checkAmbientDisjoint(socket, ambient); err != nil {\n90|\t\treturn \"\", err\n91|\t}\n92|\treturn socket, nil\n93|}\n94|\n95|// checkAmbientDisjoint refuses the degenerate case where an ambient\n96|// value already names the derived socket: using the socket then\n97|// would be indistinguishable from reusing the ambient server, so\n98|// acquisition refuses instead of proceeding on an ambiguous fact.\n99|// The comparison runs over cleaned spellings, so an ambient value\n100|// that names the socket through a `/./` segment or a doubled\n101|// separator refuses like the byte-identical spelling; the TMUX\n102|// member compares its socket component, because tmux(1) encodes that\n103|// variable as `<socket>,<pid>,<index>`. A symlink alias of the root\n104|// that resolves to the same socket is not detected and stays a\n105|// stated bound.\n106|func checkAmbientDisjoint(socket string, ambient Ambient) error {\n107|\tfor _, candidate := range []string{\n108|\t\ttmuxEnvSocket(ambient.TMUXEnv),\n109|\t\tambient.TMUXTmpDir,\n110|\t\tambient.InheritedSocket,\n111|\t\tambient.DefaultPath,\n112|\t\tambient.ConventionalName,\n113|\t} {\n114|\t\tif candidate != \"\" && filepath.Clean(candidate) == socket {\n115|\t\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeAmbientReuse, Detail: \"ambient collision\"}\n116|\t\t}\n117|\t}\n118|\treturn nil\n119|}\n120|\n121|// tmuxEnvSocket returns the socket component of a TMUX environment\n122|// value, which tmux(1) encodes as `<socket>,<pid>,<index>`: the\n123|// substring before the first comma. A value without a comma compares\n124|// whole, and an empty component compares as absent.\n125|func tmuxEnvSocket(value string) string {\n126|\tif i := strings.IndexByte(value, ','); i >= 0 {\n127|\t\treturn value[:i]\n128|\t}\n129|\treturn value\n130|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c819","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":615,"recorded_at":1780531400001225,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"call_id":"call_01a0c4adb79e7498b80621f2340de1c3","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/runtime.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"os\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/secprim\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// RuntimeDirName is the fixed leaf name of the AX tmux runtime\n12|// directory under the Runtime IPC root: pinned SPEC 806-808 selects\n13|// the dedicated server by `tmux -S <runtime>/tmux/ax.sock`, so the\n14|// leaf is `tmux`. It is AX-controlled vocabulary, never an ambient\n15|// or conventional tmux name.\n16|const RuntimeDirName = \"tmux\"\n17|\n18|// Hooks arms the crash boundaries of EnsureRuntimeDir. AfterMkdir\n19|// runs after the mkdir attempt resolves — the leaf created or\n20|// already present — and before verification and the parent fsync; a\n21|// crash there must leave a retry that converges to the one verified\n22|// directory. Hooks is nil in production.\n23|type Hooks struct {\n24|\tAfterMkdir func(dir string)\n25|}\n26|\n27|// EnsureRuntimeDir creates the owner-only runtime directory\n28|// root/name when absent and verifies it when present, returning the\n29|// joined path. Creation and verification enforce three independent\n30|// gates — containment, mode, ownership — and each refuses alone:\n31|//\n32|//   - containment: the root must be an absolute path on the platform\n33|//     grammar, the name must be one relative segment, and the commit\n34|//     opens the parent through a pinned directory handle and creates\n35|//     the leaf relative to that handle, so a symlinked intermediate\n36|//     directory cannot redirect the commit outside the root;\n37|//   - mode: the leaf must carry exactly 0700, enforced explicitly\n38|//     after creation because mkdir honors umask;\n39|//   - ownership: the leaf must belong to the effective UID.\n40|//\n41|// Lexical validation delegates to its landed owners (absolute root\n42|// and relative member to scalar, the join to secprim.Guard); the\n43|// descriptor-relative commit below is what this package owns, because\n44|// no landed helper commits a directory relative to a handle.\n45|//\n46|// On failure the returned path distinguishes the refusal phase: a\n47|// lexical refusal returns \"\", while a commit-phase refusal returns\n48|// the joined path alongside the error. Callers must check the error\n49|// first and never use the path when it is set; the split lets the\n50|// acquisition wiring narrow exactly the commit-phase class.\n51|func EnsureRuntimeDir(root, name string, platform scalar.Platform, hooks *Hooks) (string, error) {\n52|\tjoined, err := lexicalRuntimePath(root, name, platform)\n53|\tif err != nil {\n54|\t\treturn \"\", err\n55|\t}\n56|\treturn joined, commitRuntimeDir(root, name, joined, hooks)\n57|}\n58|\n59|// VerifyRuntimeDir enforces the three custody gates on an existing\n60|// runtime directory without creating it. Background acquisition calls\n61|// this instead of Ensure: the directory must already exist with exact\n62|// custody, and a missing directory refuses rather than being silently\n63|// created on the authorizing path. Foreground acquisition calls\n64|// Ensure, which provisions the directory it then verifies.\n65|func VerifyRuntimeDir(root, name string, platform scalar.Platform) error {\n66|\tif _, err := lexicalRuntimePath(root, name, platform); err != nil {\n67|\t\treturn err\n68|\t}\n69|\treturn verifyRuntimeDir(root, name)\n70|}\n71|\n72|// lexicalRuntimePath validates the root grammar, the name grammar,\n73|// and the lexical join. It answers the lexical question only; the\n74|// commit answers the filesystem question through a handle.\n75|func lexicalRuntimePath(root, name string, platform scalar.Platform) (string, error) {\n76|\tif _, err := scalar.ParsePlatform(string(platform)); err != nil {\n77|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"runtime platform\"}\n78|\t}\n79|\t// Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection\n80|\t// (pinned SPEC 1458), so the Windows platform refuses here on\n81|\t// every host, before any host-specific commit runs. Weakening\n82|\t// this arm reroutes a Windows request to the root refusal\n83|\t// instead of admitting it.\n84|\tif platform == scalar.PlatformWindows {\n85|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"runtime platform\"}\n86|\t}\n87|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseAbsolutePath(platform, root); err != nil {\n88|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"runtime root\"}\n89|\t}\n90|\tif err := checkRuntimeName(name); err != nil {\n91|\t\treturn \"\", err\n92|\t}\n93|\tguard, err := secprim.NewGuard(root, platform, []string{name})\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeUnsafeRuntimeDir, Detail: \"runtime containment\"}\n96|\t}\n97|\tjoined, err := guard.Resolve(name)\n98|\tif err != nil {\n99|\t\treturn \"\", &Error{Code: CodeUnsafeRuntimeDir, Detail: \"runtime containment\"}\n100|\t}\n101|\treturn joined, nil\n102|}\n103|\n104|// checkRuntimeName admits exactly one relative path segment. The\n105|// shared grammar (absolute, parent, dot, empty, NUL, backslash,\n106|// encoded separators) is decided by scalar; this gate adds only the\n107|// single-segment rule scalar does not own, because the commit opens\n108|// the leaf relative to the pinned parent handle and a second segment\n109|// would name a path the handle walk never descends.\n110|func checkRuntimeName(name string) error {\n111|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseRelativePath(name); err != nil {\n112|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"runtime name\"}\n113|\t}\n114|\tif strings.Contains(name, \"/\") {\n115|\t\treturn &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"runtime name\"}\n116|\t}\n117|\treturn nil\n118|}\n119|\n120|// sameDirectory compares two stat results for directory identity. It\n121|// is a variable only so seam-failure tests can force the\n122|// handle-mismatch path through the production entries: a handle that\n123|// names a different directory than the path cannot be staged without\n124|// a filesystem race, and without the seam the mismatch branch is\n125|// untestable. Production code never reassigns it.\n126|var sameDirectory = os.SameFile\n127|\n128|// handleBoundToPath reports whether the open directory handle refers\n129|// to the same directory as rootPath. It mirrors the private\n130|// secprim.guardRootMatches check, which no caller outside secprim\n131|// can invoke: a stat failure on either side is not a match, and an\n132|// unreadable root fails closed into the mismatch refusal rather\n133|// than admitting an unverifiable handle.\n134|func handleBoundToPath(handle *os.File, rootPath string) bool {\n135|\thandleInfo, err := handle.Stat()\n136|\tif err != nil || handleInfo == nil {\n137|\t\treturn false\n138|\t}\n139|\tpathInfo, err := os.Stat(rootPath)\n140|\tif err != nil || pathInfo == nil {\n141|\t\treturn false\n142|\t}\n143|\treturn sameDirectory(handleInfo, pathInfo)\n144|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
