{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c84b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":640,"recorded_at":1780531400001275,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"call_id":"call_01a0c4adc1d573eb92742524c740f35f","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/tmuxserver.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer tests must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence; row D-background-fallback\n8|is the one explicitly supplementary additive plant (the reviewer-shaped\n9|direct-creation call on the background path), labeled as such and not\n10|counted as any gate's narrowing.\n11|\n12|Each row runs M (mutate production files in place), R (run the scoped Go\n13|killers through the production entries), V (verdict from the Go exit code\n14|plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line,\n15|SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else -- unapplied patches,\n16|build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are\n17|ERROR, never kills or survivals. Files are restored from backups after\n18|every row, pass or fail.\n19|\n20|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that must\n21|SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n22|hard-coding kills.\n23|\n24|Usage:\n25|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n26|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py N-mode-create\n27|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py --log-dir /tmp/mutant-logs\n28|  AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py N-mode-create\n29|\"\"\"\n30|\n31|import os\n32|import shutil\n33|import subprocess\n34|import sys\n35|import tempfile\n36|from dataclasses import dataclass\n37|from pathlib import Path\n38|\n39|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n40|PACKAGE = \"internal/tmuxserver\"\n41|\n42|\n43|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n44|class Mutant:\n45|    name: str\n46|    path: str\n47|    find: str\n48|    replace: str\n49|    count: int\n50|    run: str\n51|    expect: str\n52|    note: str\n53|\n54|\n55|BG_MISS = \"TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable\"\n56|BG_MISS_LINUX = \"(TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable|TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback)\"\n57|OVERRIDE = \"TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector\"\n58|WIDENED = \"TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode\"\n59|COLLISION = \"(TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision|TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision)\"\n60|\n61|MUTANTS = [\n62|    Mutant(\n63|        name=\"N-mode-create\",\n64|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/runtime_unix.go\",\n65|        find=\"\\t// leaf above; the mode comparison below is the load-bearing\\n\\t// arm this gate's tests and mutants pin.\\n\\tif info.Mode().Perm() != 0o700 {\\n\",\n66|        replace=\"\\t// leaf above; the mode comparison below is the load-bearing\\n\\t// arm this gate's tests and mutants pin.\\n\\tif info.Mode().Perm() != 0o700 && info.Mode().Perm() != 0o755 {\\n\",\n67|        count=1,\n68|        run=WIDENED,\n69|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n70|        note=\"Admits exactly 0755 at the create-path mode arm; other widened modes still refuse. Kill path: Ensure stops refusing.\",\n71|    ),\n72|    Mutant(\n73|        name=\"N-mode-verify\",\n74|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/runtime_unix.go\",\n75|        find='\\tinfo, err := leaf.Sta