{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":836,"recorded_at":1780531400001667,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4af-9ae8-7572-a525-d9b0329256af"},"task_id":"01a0c4af-9ae8-7572-a525-d9b0329256af","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4af-9ae8-7572-a525-d9b0329256af","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/errors.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|// Local refusal codes. The spec names capability_unavailable for the\n4|// background broker-or-refuse path (emitted through axerror with its\n5|// typed details); the codes below name the package-local safety gates\n6|// the spec states as MUST NOT rules without assigning a wire code.\n7|// Tests assert the literal strings, never these constants.\n8|const (\n9|\t// CodeAmbientReuse refuses an explicit socket override: the only\n10|\t// admissible server socket is the one derived from the runtime\n11|\t// directory, so any caller-supplied socket (ambient environment\n12|\t// value, inherited socket, default path, or conventional name)\n13|\t// refuses instead of redirecting acquisition.\n14|\tCodeAmbientReuse = \"tmux_ambient_server_reuse\"\n15|\t// CodeBackgroundCreationRefused refuses direct server creation\n16|\t// on the background path. A background caller never creates; it\n17|\t// contacts the broker or receives capability_unavailable.\n18|\tCodeBackgroundCreationRefused = \"tmux_background_creation_refused\"\n19|\t// CodeUnsafeRuntimeDir refuses a runtime directory that fails\n20|\t// any of the three custody gates: mode, ownership, containment.\n21|\tCodeUnsafeRuntimeDir = \"tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir\"\n22|\t// CodeReadinessNotAuthorizing refuses an authorization attempt\n23|\t// backed only by a diagnostic hint or a cached observation.\n24|\tCodeReadinessNotAuthorizing = \"tmux_readiness_not_authorizing\"\n25|\t// CodeInvalidArguments refuses a malformed acquisition request:\n26|\t// unknown caller, unknown platform, malformed generation, or\n27|\t// missing typed-detail members.\n28|\tCodeInvalidArguments = \"tmux_invalid_arguments\"\n29|\t// CodeSpawnFailed reports a dedicated-server spawn failure.\n30|\t// The spawner is caller-supplied; this code carries no fallback.\n31|\tCodeSpawnFailed = \"tmux_server_spawn_failed\"\n32|)\n33|\n34|// Error is a package-local refusal. Code is one of the Code*\n35|// constants; Detail is a static clause naming the gate. It never\n36|// echoes paths, socket names, generations, or environment values.\n37|type Error struct {\n38|\tCode   string\n39|\tDetail string\n40|}\n41|\n42|func (err *Error) Error() string {\n43|\treturn \"tmux server refused: \" + err.Code + \" at \" + err.Detail\n44|}","final_result":true}}}
