{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d3ab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c4ab-e99a-71a1-b01c-d4e1f789add0"},"sequence":2096,"recorded_at":1780531400004187,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e9eaa535-0e9f-444e-ac97-d216243d9df7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c4c3-8159-73d0-9641-dfe111d011e9"},"task_id":"01a0c4c3-8159-73d0-9641-dfe111d011e9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c4c3-8159-73d0-9641-dfe111d011e9","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-21\n-\n-### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\n+## 2026-09-21\n+\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\n+\n+- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev4 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, two P2, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev3 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). P2-A: `requireLocalError` now asserts the TOP-LEVEL `*Error` (plus no reachable `*axerror.Error`), because `errors.As` looked through the `capability_unavailable` wrapper whose cause is redacted off the wire — the new `N-absence-remap-widen` (the reviewer's R05 shape: `runtimeAbsent` admitting `runtime mode`) SURVIVES under the old helper and KILLS under the fixed one, proven by replay; `N-background-absence-remap` kept for the other direction. Re-ran every custody row after the oracle change: none only passed because of the old helper.\n+- P2-B: `Request.Name` is DELETED — the acquisition entry always passes `RuntimeDirName`, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths with no per-call spelling that can re-open the `§3.2` divergence (the reviewer's P01 probe is unstageable: the field does not exist; R11 is inapplicable). `TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath` asserts the literal `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` through `Acquire` for foreground and background, named under rows 16/56. P3-A: `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating` now drives macos/linux/wsl2 subtests (the reviewer's R14 shape fails on linux+wsl2 firsthand, named under row 52). P3-B: the four unarmed background tests now arm the spy, and the README/`acquire.go` sentence is scoped to background-path `Acquire` tests — mechanical census: 12/12 armed.\n+- Observations: row 6 states the ELOOP darwin-equivalence (reasoned, not run); B15 gains the unopenable-root arm and the `Fchmod`/`Fsync`/leaf-`Stat` arms; B16 states the nested-invocation over-strict refusal (owner: TASK-260830-1c28dz); row 23 scopes the live collision members to `TMUXEnv`/`InheritedSocket`; B19 states the `localstore`-root caller contract as undriven.\n+- Battery: 55 narrowing + 1 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 57/57 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev5). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race in bounded groups, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\n","final_result":true}}}
